{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/general-onyx-path-discussion/1548629-world-of-final-fantasy-darkness","id":1548629,"title":"World of Final Fantasy Darkness????","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","General Onyx Path Discussion"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-02-20T12:53:01-08:00","id":1548629,"title":"World of Final Fantasy Darkness????","content":"I am a huge fan of Final Fantasy series. I am also, a HUGE fan of Werewolf the Apocalypse game, and, to the lesser extend of other WOD games. Unfortunately it is VERY hard to find a good Changelling game. Probably the hardest one to run as well. Even very long ago I noticed several things:<br /> a) Huge corporation is destroying the earth itself and the earth is SCREAMING in pain. (I wonder where did I see this before?)<br /> b) The very same corporation is doing experiments with humans and animals turning humans (sometimes) into a super soldiers, but they pay for it with various mental issues, corruption and shortened lifespan (Where have I seen that before?)<br /> c) There is a group of Eco Terrorists attacking the assets of the company whenever they can. (Where have I seen that before?)<br /> d) There is an essence that gives life to all and is also a source of magic and magick of all kinds (Where have I seen that before?)<br /> e) Occasionally there are monsters from &quot;The other side&quot; materialize in the real world and either corrupt people and nature or run amok (Where have I seen that before?)<br /> What I am trying to say is that there are a LOT of similarities between Final Fantasy 7 and the world of Werewolf the Apocalypse.<br /> Genetically enchanced soldiers infused with &quot;strange&quot; energy that turns them insane and twists them? S.O.L.D.I.E.R (Which makes them a FOMORI)<br /> The difference between Pentex and Shinra are minimal. Differences between Shinra and N.W.O./Technocracy is also minimal, just take a look at the mechs. Airbuster = Hitmark<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> First team = Turks<br /> Avalanche = Your average Garou Pack. fighting Pentex.<br /> Lifestream - Gnosis/Quintessense<br /> Am I the only one noticing those similarities? I am NOT saying that one setting copied another, but the similarities land to borrowing from one setting to another. <br /> <br /> <br /> My question is this. Has anyone ever seen World of Darkness rules be converted into Final Fantasy setting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26712-tigerclaw_x","name":"Tigerclaw_x","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-21T12:38:01-08:00","id":1548684,"title":"","content":"The barrier between video games and ttrpgs was a bit thicker back in those days, and by the time W20 was out and more people would have been up to it, FF7 was kind of rather far in the back mirror. I think someone may have certainly tried a merging or conversion, but that was a rather long time ago and technically there was a little bit of everything of BJ Zanzibar's site.<br /> <br /> Also, there's no genetic tinkering in fomori or typical SOLDIER members. Just being exposed to an eerie green light or having some noxious shit attract a bane to you and a lot of abuse giving said bane an in. The &quot;enhancements&quot; of some of the more... experimental members of SOLDIER that had them repeating &quot;reunion!&quot; constantly was done courtesy of Jenova cell injections by Professor <a href=\"https://youtu.be/bwSNtPUUSKk?list=PL5j80D9V7lqZI-tK6mqcno5liPaLt9dAv&amp;t=265\" target=\"_blank\">HOJO!</a> that made them even more potent but also messed them up; the W:tA equivalent of that wouldn't be out until the W20 Book of the Wyrm. It was more like having part of an alien grafted to your system and having it slowly take over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-22T18:32:27-08:00","id":1548721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tigerclaw_x</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/general-onyx-path-discussion/1548629-world-of-final-fantasy-darkness#post1548629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question is this. Has anyone ever seen World of Darkness rules be converted into Final Fantasy setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well somewhat unrelated but my dream WtA game is basically metal gear sold, the main character is essentially Solid Snake who undergone the first change in the middle of the sneaking mission and now he has to deal with all the baggage that comes with being a garou while trying to complete the mission.<br /> <br /> Oh and he also has the traditional metal gear series end game fist fight with Calhal (who fallen way off the deep end after earthblood). Also his daughter is actually the main character's love interest/ impromptu mentor and her one of her mission is actually putting her own farther down...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-22T18:41:17-08:00","id":1548723,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'd incorporate more of Ogre Battle/Unicorn Overlord. In the former, having brutally overpowered units liberating towns can actually work against you in terms of reputation (so, the Delirium, basically), while the latter has a theme of reconciliation between cultures that have been at odds and concentration on drawing out the true threat to everyone's existence via said cooperation.<br /> <br /> (Charging ahead to the last battle stage in the latter game, without aiding any of Cornia's neighbors, is the way you get the worst ending, incidentally. And your enemy has reinforcements that you would have otherwise had, to boot.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}